Network compiled into crate stitch by burn-onnx (build.rs), under a permissive licence whose text is next to this
file, and run by burn on the shared device for the seam flow (src/raft.rs).

raft_small_128x2176.onnx
  What: RAFT-small optical flow (Teed & Deng, "RAFT: Recurrent All-Pairs Field Transforms for Optical Flow", ECCV
        2020, https://arxiv.org/abs/2003.12039), 0.99 M parameters: torchvision's Raft_Small_Weights.C_T_V2 exported
        to ONNX for src/raft.rs (128 x 2176, 8 iterations, opset 17).
  Source: https://docs.pytorch.org/vision/stable/models/generated/torchvision.models.optical_flow.raft_small.html
          (C_T_V2, the default: "These weights were trained from scratch on FlyingChairs + FlyingThings3D", recipe
          https://github.com/pytorch/vision/tree/main/references/optical_flow)
  Licence: BSD-3-Clause (torchvision) -> LICENSE-torchvision. torchvision's README: "The pre-trained models provided
           in this library may have their own licenses or terms and conditions derived from the dataset used for
           training. It is your responsibility to determine whether you have permission to use the models for your
           use case."
  Training data: FlyingChairs and FlyingThings3D (one of the Scene Flow datasets), synthetic, from the University of
           Freiburg: "provided for research purposes only and without any warranty. Any commercial use is
           prohibited." (https://lmb.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/resources/datasets/FlyingChairs.en.html and
           https://lmb.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/resources/datasets/SceneFlowDatasets.en.html, whose FAQ answers
           commercial use with "Unfortunately, this is not possible. We do not own the necessary licenses for the 3D
           models and textures which we used.")
